        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Menindee Lakes, Menindee, Menindee County, New South Wales, Australia\n- Organizations: Central Darling Shire\n- Natural features: Darling River\n\nFacts:\n- Menindee is a small town in the far west of New South Wales, Australia.\n- Menindee is frequently but incorrectly spelled \"Menindie.\"\n- Menindee is in Central Darling Shire and lies on the banks of the Darling River.\n- Menindee had a sign-posted population of 980 and a 2011 census population of 449.\n- Menindee Lakes lie in the far west region of New South Wales, Australia, near the town of Menindee.\n- Menindee Lakes are located in Menindee County.",
